room marrow_cabin "The Marrow — Captain's Cabin"
  bg bg_cabin_wide
  width 2560
  music music_office
  # Measured from the plate: the chart table is ~290 px tall with its front edge at y≈450, so a
  # standing adult is ~600 px here (the table then sits at the waist). The cabin is a close room;
  # its people are large.
  perspective horizon 200 ref 875 height 430
  scale 700 560
  scale 800 600
  scale 875 630
  # The stern window's sill and step run from x≈1840 to the right wall; keep Fenn on the
  # planking in front of them rather than standing in the open window.
  walk (80,875) (140,700) (1800,700) (1840,820) (2380,820) (2420,875)
  entry 1900,845
  arrive marrow_quarterdeck 2300,845
  arrive marrow_gallery 2100,845

  # Atmosphere: the cabin lantern, and the sea moving past the stern windows.
  footsteps deck
  light 1160,45 radius 200 lantern
  water (1915,240) (2325,240) (2325,690) (1915,690) ripple 1.5
  emit creak

  sprite npc_vane_body at 1520,806 size 1 idle speaker vane for vane grade "saturate(0.85) brightness(0.9)"

  # Out on the stern gallery Vane is there and not here (marrow_gallery.adv sets vane_out).
  on enter
    set vane_out = false

  hotspot chart "chart table"
    area 940,310 800x260
    stand 1150,810
    look "The Straits, inked to look manageable. A pencil line runs north of the reef, the long way round. Pell's line, and the captain's."
    use "I'd need something to take a bearing with. Something that points where it likes."
    state if vane_terms
      look "Pell's pencil line, north of the reef. Beside it, faint and new, a second line straight through. Not mine. Vane's."

  hotspot windows "stern windows"
    area 1150,30 780x270
    nowalk
    look "The wake, going back the way we came, to a harbour I can't see any more. Every reason I took this berth is in that white water."

  # The open stern window, out to the captain's gallery (marrow_gallery.adv): optional, open
  # once she has named her terms, shut again when she goes up to the wheel.
  hotspot gallery "the stern gallery"
    area 1905,30 420x655
    stand 2100,845
    look "Beyond the stern window, the captain's gallery, over the wake. Hers. Nobody goes out uninvited, and nobody's invited."
    walk "Vane's gallery. Without an invitation I'd only be a clerk on a balcony, being looked at."
    open "Vane's gallery. Without an invitation I'd only be a clerk on a balcony, being looked at."
    state if vane_convinced
      look "The captain's gallery. Not now: the fog's coming, and I'm wanted at the bow."
      walk "No time for the view. The bow, the bearings, the fog."
      open "No time for the view. The bow, the bearings, the fog."
    state if vane_terms
      exit marrow_gallery
      look "The captain's gallery, over the wake. Quill says she drinks her rum out there alone. Never asks anyone. She said it like a dare."

  hotspot bunk "the bunk"
    area 0,180 330x440
    nowalk
    look "A bunk, with the corners of a woman who has made it herself for years. Under the pillow, a romance novel, face down and well read."
      say "Its bookmark is a letter from an insurance office, which says something about both."

  hotspot door_out "door to the quarterdeck"
    area 2400,200 160x560
    stand 2340,845
    exit marrow_quarterdeck
    look "The door back out to the quarterdeck."

  # After the chart table, so it wins where she stands in front of it.
  hotspot vane "Captain Vane"
    show if not vane_convinced and not vane_out
    area 1430,200 190x600
    stand 1690,800
    look "Captain Vane. She has the coat of a woman who has been rich and the eyes of one who has been poor since."
    talk "She looks up from the chart with the expression of someone interrupting herself."
      talk vane
    give "She looks at it, then at me, and waits for me to put it away."

  use compass on chart if not vane_terms
    "I set the compass on the chart. The needle swings past north and settles on a line straight through the reef. Vane comes round the table very slowly."
    talk vane at compass
  use compass on chart
    "The needle still points straight through the reef. Vane doesn't need to see it again. She needs three reasons."
  use pell_log on vane if vane_terms and quill_navigator and crew_agree
    "I put Pell's log on the chart table, open at the last page. Vane doesn't look down at it. She knows the handwriting from here."
    talk vane at log
  use pell_log on vane if vane_terms
    "She puts a hand flat on the log without opening it. “Not yet, clerk. A navigator and a crew first. Then you can break my heart.”"
  use pell_log on vane
    "Her face shuts like a hatch. “That's Pell's. Put it back where you found it.”"
  use sextant on vane
    "“Pell's sextant.” She doesn't take it. “Give it to someone who can use it. I have someone in mind. So, I suspect, do you.”"
  use manifest on vane
    "She reads the names and hands it back. “Twenty-two. I know where you're going with that, clerk. Take it below, to someone who'll go there with you.”"
  use compass on vane if not vane_terms
    "She doesn't look at it. “Show me on the chart, clerk. I don't take bearings off people's palms.”"
  use compass on vane
    "“I've seen where it points. Now bring me three reasons it's allowed to.”"
